---

1. MAIN FEATURES

* uv: Incredibly fast environment and package management (replacement for pip, pip-tools, and venv).


https://docs.astral.sh/uv/ 


* Nuitka: Compiler that transforms Python code and its dependencies into an executable binary.


https://nuitka.net/ 


* Performance and Portability: Deploys a single binary file, ideal for environments without pre-installed Python.

---

2. REQUIREMENTS
Make sure you have the following installed:

* uv: Installed globally.

  Bash

# uv installation (using curl or pipx)
    curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | 
sh 
    # Or
    pipx install uv

* uv sync: To synchronize dependencies within each example project.


* uv pip list: To list installed dependencies.


* Nuitka: Will be installed as a development dependency that   automatically synchronizes with uv sync, but sometimes requires system compilation tools (like gcc or Visual Studio Build Tools).

3. INSTALLATION (with uv)

Clone the repository and use uv to set up your development environment:

Bash

# 1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/KRRT7/compile-me.git
cd compile-me

# 2. Initialize the virtual environment and resolve dependencies
# uv reads pyproject.toml and automatically creates the .venv
uv sync
---

4. USAGE AND DEVELOPMENT

Once the environment is activated and dependencies are synchronized, you can run the application with:

Bash

# uv run


5. COMPILING TO BINARY (with Nuitka)
To generate a standalone executable that includes everything needed to run the API without external dependencies:

Bash

# Standalone binary compilation command with Nuitka
uv run nuitka \
  --standalone \
  --follow-imports \
  --output-dir=dist \
  --include-package=uvicorn.server \
  --plugin-enable=pyside6 \
  app/main.py

Result: The binary executable and its dependencies will be found in the dist/main.onefile.exe folder (the name may vary depending on the OS).

Running the Binary

Bash

# Execute the compiled binary (Linux/macOS example)
./dist/app.bin.dist/app.main
# Or on Windows:
.\dist\app.main.exe

# Onefile binary compilation command (--onefile) with Nuitka
uv run nuitka --onefile main.py

